---
layout: base.njk
title: "Wire flow in 3D — Pragmatic Agents Lab"
description: "An interactive 3D model of institutional wire processing: drag straight-through processing from 0% to 99.9% and raise the volume to see why the manual desk stops scaling."
permalink: /lab/wire-flow/
---
<style>
/* The stage is a dark room inside the light page: glow needs a dark ground to read as depth. */
.wf-wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 40px; }
.wf-stage { position: relative; height: min(68vh, 640px); min-height: 400px; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; background: #100D0A; margin-top: 28px; touch-action: none; }
.wf-stage canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; cursor: grab; }
.wf-stage canvas:active { cursor: grabbing; }
.wf-labels { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; overflow: hidden; }
.wf-label { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; text-align: center; white-space: nowrap; font-family: var(--sans); line-height: 1.25; will-change: transform; text-shadow: 0 1px 6px #100D0A, 0 0 2px #100D0A; }
.wf-label strong { display: block; font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; color: #F3EBDD; }
.wf-label span { display: block; font-size: 10.5px; color: #A79C8B; }
.wf-label.wf-auto strong { color: #F0C27A; }
.wf-label.wf-manual strong { color: #B5C4D4; }
.wf-label-layer { text-align: left; }
.wf-label-layer strong { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; }
.wf-label-layer span { font-size: 9.5px; }
.wf-label-title strong { font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: .02em; }
.wf-views { position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 12px; display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.wf-views button { font: 600 11.5px var(--sans); color: #E9DFCE; background: rgba(30,25,19,.72); border: 1px solid rgba(233,223,206,.22); border-radius: 5px; padding: 6px 11px; cursor: pointer; }
.wf-views button:hover, .wf-views button.active { border-color: #E2AD62; color: #F0C27A; }
.wf-views button:focus-visible, .wf-buttons button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #E2AD62; outline-offset: 2px; }
.wf-hint { position: absolute; right: 12px; bottom: 10px; font-size: 11.5px; color: #A79C8B; pointer-events: none; }
.wf-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 18px 36px; margin-top: 20px; align-items: end; }
.wf-ctl label { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 6px; }
.wf-ctl output { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--accent-ink); }
.wf-ctl input[type=range] { width: 100%; accent-color: var(--accent); }
.wf-buttons { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.wf-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 22px; }
.wf-stat { border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-strong); padding-top: 10px; }
.wf-stat b { display: block; font-family: var(--heading); font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--text); }
.wf-stat b.wf-hot { color: #B03030; }
.wf-stat span { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
.wf-notes { max-width: 700px; margin-top: 34px; }
.wf-notes p { margin-bottom: 14px; }
.wf-notes .wf-small { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }
@media (max-width: 640px) { .wf-wrap { padding: 0 18px; } .wf-stage { height: 540px; } .wf-label span, .wf-label-layer { display: none; } .wf-label strong { font-size: 11px; } }
</style>

<div class="wf-wrap">
  <section>
    <span class="kicker">Lab · interactive model</span>
    <h1>Wire flow, from the manual desk to <span class="hl">99.9% straight through</span></h1>
    <p class="sub">Each point of light is a payment. Straight-through payments climb the platform, pass the SWIFT ring and arc to the banks. The rest drop to the operations desk and wait. Drag the sliders, then orbit the scene.</p>

    <div class="wf-stage" id="wf-stage">
      <canvas id="wf-canvas" aria-label="3D scene: payments rise from three source pillars and either climb a layered automation platform, pass a SWIFT ring and arc to four bank towers, or drop to a manual operations desk where they pile up"></canvas>
      <div class="wf-labels" id="wf-labels"></div>
      <div class="wf-views">
        <button data-wf-view="overview">Overview</button>
        <button data-wf-view="platform">Platform</button>
        <button data-wf-view="desk">Desk</button>
        <button data-wf-view="banks">Banks</button>
        <button id="wf-orbit" class="active">Orbit</button>
      </div>
      <span class="wf-hint">Drag to orbit · scroll to zoom · right-drag to pan</span>
    </div>

    <div class="wf-panel">
      <div class="wf-ctl">
        <label for="wf-stp">Straight-through processing <output id="wf-stp-out">99.9%</output></label>
        <input type="range" id="wf-stp" min="0" max="999" value="999" step="1">
      </div>
      <div class="wf-ctl">
        <label for="wf-vol">Payment volume <output id="wf-vol-out">×1</output></label>
        <input type="range" id="wf-vol" min="1" max="18" value="1" step="1">
      </div>
      <div class="wf-buttons">
        <button class="arch-btn active" id="wf-journey">Play the journey: 0% to 99.9%</button>
        <button class="arch-btn" id="wf-play">Pause</button>
        <button class="arch-btn" id="wf-reset">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wf-stats">
      <div class="wf-stat"><b id="wf-auto">0</b><span>settled straight through</span></div>
      <div class="wf-stat"><b id="wf-manual">0</b><span>settled by hand</span></div>
      <div class="wf-stat"><b id="wf-queue">0</b><span>waiting at the desk</span></div>
      <div class="wf-stat"><b id="wf-rework">0</b><span>sent back for rework</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="wf-notes">
      <p><strong>What to try.</strong> Set straight-through processing to 0% and volume to ×18. The desk has four people, the heap keeps growing and the queue never clears. Now drag processing back to 99.9% at the same volume: the platform absorbs it and the desk handles only the exceptions.</p>
      <p>That is the argument of the <a href="/work/wire-automation/">wire automation case study</a>: the real programme went from 0% to 99%+ straight-through processing and absorbed roughly 18× volume growth without adding headcount.</p>
      <p class="wf-small">This is an illustrative simulation. Speeds, error rates and queue sizes are chosen to show the mechanism and are not client data.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

